## 2. Portal member namespace (`/me/*`)

### 2.1 Verified routes (implemented)

| Path | Auth | Purpose | Repo | Smoke |
| ---- | ---- | ------- | ---- | ----- |
| `/me` | member session (middleware) | **Namespace root — no page today** | Protected in `middleware.ts`; **no** `app/me/page.tsx` → 404 after auth | — |
| `/me/registrations` | member session | Member trip/registration list | `app/me/registrations/page.tsx` | SMK-PTL-02, SMK-PTL-05 |
| `/me/registrations/{id}` | member session | Detail + receipt upload | `app/me/registrations/[id]/page.tsx` | SMK-PTL-04 |
| `/me/profile` | member session | Capability-driven profile edit | `app/me/profile/page.tsx` | SMK-PTL-07 |

**WRS-PATH-02 unchanged:** Portal has **no** `/tours`. Public catalog browsing remains marketing-only.

### 2.2 Bare `/me` policy (DL-40) — planned

| Request | Current behavior | Target behavior |
| ------- | ---------------- | --------------- |
| `GET /me` + valid session | Middleware passes → **404** (no page) | **302** → `defaultPrimaryModuleId` route |
| `GET /me` + no session | Middleware → `/` | Unchanged |

`/me` is a **namespace root only** — never a content page.

### 2.3 Portal root `/` (verified)

| Session | Behavior | Repo |
| ------- | -------- | ---- |
| Guest | Redirect to marketing public base (GSH) | `app/page.tsx` |
| Member | **Hardcoded** redirect to `/me/registrations` | `app/page.tsx` L12 |

**Target (DL-06):** Redirect to `defaultPrimaryModuleId` from member registry; `/me/registrations` remains permanent alias.

### 2.4 Registration (outside member shell)

| Path | Auth | Shell mode | Repo |
| ---- | ---- | ---------- | ---- |
| `/catalog/{tourId}/register` | public-auth session | **Minimal** — no bottom nav (DL-01) | `app/catalog/[tourId]/register/page.tsx` |

**Invariant:** Registration paths **never** move under `/me/*` (DL-01, DL-42).

### 2.5 Portal BFF routes (verified)

| Path | Auth | Purpose |
| ---- | ---- | ------- |
| `GET /api/me/registrations` | member | List proxy → `GET /bookings?view=mine` |
| `POST /api/me/registrations/{id}/receipt` | member | Receipt upload BFF |
| `GET/PATCH /api/me/profile` | member | Profile BFF (PCMS profile freeze) |
| `POST /api/public-auth/logout` | none (idempotent) | Clear `atour_mb_session` |
| `POST /api/public-auth/*` | varies | OTP / register-complete (P6-1) |

**Planned (RFC, not in repo):**

| Path | Purpose | Decision |
| ---- | ------- | -------- |
| `GET /api/me/entitlements` | Nav ∩ registry gating | DL-09 |
| `GET /api/me/home` | Home module aggregate | DL-19 |

Semantics: [member-session-portal-authority.mdoc](./member-session-portal-authority.mdoc), [platform-portal-member.mdoc](../phase-19/platform-portal-member.mdoc).

---

## 3. Future module routing (planned — not implemented)

Member Application Platform adds manifest-driven modules under `/me/*`.

### 3.1 Module id vs route (DL-03, DL-30)

| Module id | Route | Status | Owner |
| --------- | ----- | ------ | ----- |
| `trips` | `/me/registrations` | **Alias frozen** | Workspace |
| `profile` | `/me/profile` | Implemented | Workspace |
| `home` | `/me/home` | Planned BP-4 | **Platform-owned** — workspace MUST NOT declare |
| `wallet`, `membership`, … | `/me/{id}` | Planned | Workspace |
| `{moduleId}` | manifest `routePath` | Planned BP-5+ | Workspace |

#### Reserved module ids (DL-30)

**Platform-owned (platform delivers module; workspace MUST NOT declare in manifest):**

| id | Route | Notes |
| -- | ----- | ----- |
| `home` | `/me/home` | Denali bottom-nav “Home” references platform module |

**Namespace-reserved (codegen blocklist — not a deliverable module):**

| id | Reason |
| -- | ------ |
| `more` | Shell “More” hub slot |
| `api` | BFF `/api/me/*` namespace |
| `catalog` | Registration `/catalog/*` namespace |

**Validation:** `guard-member-module-id-reserved` fails workspace manifest entries for any id above.

**No conflict:** `/me/home` is a **route**; `home` is a **reserved module id** owned by the platform. Workspaces may list `home` in nav tier ordering via generated effective registry — they do not declare the module block.

### 3.2 Navigation tiers (member shell)

| Tier | Max | Example |
| ---- | --- | ------- |
| Primary | 5 | Bottom nav: Home, Trips, Wallet, Membership, More |
| Secondary | N | More hub |
| Hidden | N | Deep link only |
| Cross-surface | N | Header egress → marketing |

**Codegen rule (DL-04):** >5 primary modules → fail-closed.

### 3.3 Dynamic dispatcher (DL-24, DL-28)

| Phase | Routing strategy |
| ----- | ---------------- |
| 1–4 | Static `app/me/{module}/page.tsx` folders |
| 5+ | `app/me/[[...modulePath]]/page.tsx` dispatcher |
| Always | Static routes **win** over catch-all |

**Reserved module ids (DL-30):** See §3.1 — `home` is platform-owned; `more`, `api`, `catalog` are namespace-reserved.

**Not planned on portal:** `/me/catalog/*`, `/me/tours/*` — violates WRS-PATH-02.

